<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kavan Tissa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Kakavannatissa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kavan Tissa was a king of Ruhuna in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> in the 2nd century BCE, known from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahavamsa">Mahavamsa</a> chronicle. Ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tissamaharama">Mahagama</a>, he strengthened the southern kingdom and married Viharamahadevi. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutugemunu">Dutugemunu</a> later defeated the Tamil king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ellalan">Elara</a> and united the island under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anuradhapura">Anuradhapura</a>.</p></div>
